{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:96cc4232c1dbba92","name":"J9 Worker Drone","source":{"id":"source:reference-96cc4232c1dbba92","title":"J9 Worker Drone","revision":19695,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:26:19Z","sha256":"71a6ccfa3e1eb2c038c6eb2d6c7611fd078483fc84d44c88e678b6757793d95f","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19695","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=J9%20Worker%20Drone&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-96cc4232c1dbba92","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scum and Villainy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scum_and_Villainy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When the Roche Hive introduced its J9 Worker Drone onto the open market, the Droid was an instant failure. Though designed as a Protocol Droid, the J9's insectoid appearance and bland moniker were disliked by the majority of the mammalian ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"}," in the galaxy. Only after failing to market the Droid to other insectoid ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"}," did the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Verpine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Verpine","referenceId":"reference:216c2b50aac221ae"}," slash the price of new J9s in an attempt to sell the model. J9s purchased at such prices were often put to work as laborers, given that the typical customer's need for a Protocol Droid was low to nonexistent.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Despite the J9's advanced processor and potential effectiveness in a diplomatic role, most purchasers assumed that \"Worker Drone\" was a literal indication of the unit's intended use. Their personalities are unexciting, albeit stable.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["J9 Worker Drones can be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"ht